{
  "_notes": "M5 sound. Every effect is synthesized in code by src/audio.js from the classic sfxr parameter model (no audio files): wave = square | saw | sine | triangle | noise; attack / sustain / punch / decay = envelope (0..1, squared into sample counts like sfxr); freq = base frequency (0..1, sfxr scale), freq_limit = cutoff that stops the sound when the slide reaches it, slide / dslide = frequency ramp and its ramp; vib_strength / vib_speed = vibrato; arp_mod / arp_speed = the one-step arpeggio (positive = jump up, negative = jump down, arp_speed = when); duty / duty_ramp = square-wave duty; repeat_speed = retrigger; pha_offset / pha_ramp = phaser; lpf_freq / lpf_ramp / lpf_resonance = low-pass; hpf_freq / hpf_ramp = high-pass; volume = 0..1. An entry may instead be { sequence: [ { at: seconds, ...overrides } ], base: {...} } to play several sfxr notes in a row (fanfares, chimes). defaults = the Settings values on first run (persisted as browser prefs after that). ambient = the optional bed: a soft two-oscillator pad plus sparse bird chirps, all synthesized. idle_roar = how often a wandering dinosaur roars on its own (chance per move start, minimum gap in seconds). throttle_seconds = minimum gap between two plays of the same id (a burst of member joins or low-food warnings at 10x plays once, not thirty times); DPS.sfx() ignores it. arrival_roar_gain / idle_roar_gain scale the purchase roar and the wandering roar.",
